# /sdd-resume

Purpose:
  Auto-generated purpose for sdd-resume.

Owns: commands\sdd-resume.sdd
Description:
  Resume a failed or interrupted chain execution from the last
  checkpoint. Skips completed stages.

Usage:
  /sdd-resume
  /sdd-resume --chain=<id>
  /sdd-resume --checkpoint=<id>
  /sdd-resume --list

Options:
  --chain        Resume specific chain
  --checkpoint   Resume from specific checkpoint
  --list         List available checkpoints

Process:
  1. Load checkpoint
  2. Verify integrity
  3. Skip completed stages
  4. Resume from next stage

Safety:
  Current state backed up before resume.
  Human confirmation required.

Exit Codes:
  0 - Success
  1 - Failed
  2 - No checkpoint found
  3 - Checkpoint corrupted

State: +
